abstract: >-
  Systematic characterisation framework for velocity-curvature power law
  analytical protocols, evaluating six pipeline combinations ({Butterworth+
  finite-differences, Savitzky-Golay} x {OLS, Levenberg-Marquardt, IRLS})
  across 18,045,720 parameter configurations. Finds that whether a
  protocol's mapping from the true generative exponent to the recovered
  value is even invertible is a separate question from its measurement
  precision: across seven empirical datasets, only 4 of 42 dataset-pipeline
  combinations pass a local-monotonicity invertibility gate cleanly, 6 are
  conditional, and 32 fail outright. Grid inversion (the pre-registered
  design) still yields a pooled estimate of the true generator (beta_gen*
  approximately 0.30); pointwise, noise-calibrated inversion reports
  non-recoverability honestly where grid inversion is not safe to trust.
